        {
          "id": 631248800,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Fail I'm getting is:\n\n```\nLinking C executable run/extcap/sdjournal\nFAILED: run/extcap/sdjournal \n: && /bin/cc -fvisibility=hidden  -fexcess-precision=fast -Wall -Wextra -Wendif-labels -Wpointer-arith -Wformat-security -fwrapv -fno-strict-overflow -Wvla -Waddress -Wattributes -Wdiv-by-zero -Wignored-qualifiers -Wpragmas -Wno-overlength-strings -Wno-long-long -Wredundant-decls -Wframe-larger-than=32768 -fdiagnostics-color=always -Wshadow -Wold-style-definition -Wstrict-prototypes -Wlogical-op -Wjump-misses-init -Werror=implicit -Wno-missing-braces -Wno-pointer-sign -std=gnu99  -O2 -g -DNDEBUG -Wl,--as-needed  -fPIE -pie extcap/CMakeFiles/extcap-base.dir/extcap-base.c.o extcap/CMakeFiles/sdjournal.dir/sdjournal.c.o -o run/extcap/sdjournal  -Wl,-rpath,\"\\$ORIGIN/../:/app/vbuild/RHEL7-x86_64/zlib/1.2.11/lib:::::\"  run/libwiretap.so.0.0.0  run/libwritecap.a  run/libwsutil.so.0.0.0  /usr/lib64/libglib-2.0.so  /app/vbuild/RHEL7-x86_64/zlib/1.2.11/lib/libz.so  -ldl  /usr/lib64/libsystemd.so  /usr/lib64/libgmodule-2.0.so && :\n//app/vbuild/RHEL7-x86_64/libgcrypt/1.9.2/lib/libgcrypt.so.20: undefined reference to `gpg_strsource@GPG_ERROR_1.0'\n```\n\nThe fail reason is that Gcrypt is not available",
