    {
      "id": "3180bc35929dce013f4f9b0348a4b146d0c53196",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 631398942,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Can you try adding `${GCRYPT_LIBRARIES}` to `sdjournal_LIBS` in `extcap/CMakeLists.txt` instead?\n\nAs the comment in `wsutil/CMakeLists.txt` says, \"*Lots* of our targets that link with wsutil also link with GLib and GModule. Mark them PUBLIC so that dependent targets don't have to link them directly.\" We can do the same for Libgcrypt, but most of the targets that link with wsutil don't need Libgcrypt.\n\nWe can probably remove `${GLIB2_LIBRARIES}` from all of the `*_LIBS` lists in `extcap/CMakeLists.txt`, but that's a separate issue.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789948913",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
